  "changes": "LoadDenoiserWeights and loadProjectionWeights now call the existing safetensors.ReadF32 instead of independently allocating a full F32 byte buffer and manually decoding it into another full F32 array. Both old loops and their io/math imports are removed: 7 production lines added, 27 removed across the three owners; no public entrypoint, wrapper or allocator added. Denoiser F32/element validation and projection name checks remain unchanged. TextConditioning, the Wan request form and training projection preparation share the migrated projection loader. Unsupported ReadF32 dtypes are rejected before allocation; F32/F16/BF16 promotion and truncated payload errors pass the owning component tests.",
  "decision": "adopt",
  "environment": "evidence:sha256:5710a0101669421a5e90b1964419f83bf60c16ae94fec0051cb86fdbda29b196",
  "harness": "evidence:sha256:0c6b9d35651e5821c8c9a499c676a1de1908042f7f302a4c86c5bcd890810219",
  "limitations": "Measurements cover complete CPU loading only, not generation speed or GPU transfers. Each consumer uses its own process and the identical frozen first/repeat harness. Process peak is cumulative within that process; OS file cache, map iteration and other application activity remain uncontrolled. Observed CPU load was 39% before and 40% after the candidate cohort, versus 6% and 1% for the baseline. Other worktree gates remained active outside their test phases. Raw comparisons do not establish an isolated causal or population speedup. Existing small G3/G4 numerical, lifecycle and full text-conditioning references pass without changing tolerances. Full-resolution video quality, GPU transfer reuse and constrained-capacity validation remain separate open work.",
